(*!
<summary>
Beckhoff pulse train output feedback status process image.
</summary>
<description>
Requires EL2521 Standard 32-bit (MDP 253/511), TxPDOs 0x1A01 and 0x1A05.
Status and CounterStatus belong to separate PDOs; both carry sync error at bit 13 and toggle at bit 15.
Status bit 6 reports a PTO error. Evaluate bus validity and both status words before using CounterValue.
Link each input field individually; zero values do not prove valid links. Legacy and 16-bit layouts are unsupported.
Use one owner task and externally synchronize other access; copies are not atomic multi-field snapshots.
When used for I/O, link located fields or their containing buffers to the matching selected PDOs.
The record is not a packed wire buffer; compiler padding is not part of the device specification.
Unlinked/default values do not prove valid I/O. The caller evaluates bus/channel validity before use.
Use one owner task per instance and externally synchronize other access; multi-field snapshots are not atomic.
Copies store data without creating hardware links. Keep borrowed field references valid while consumers are bound.
This passive record performs no validation, synchronization, configuration or protocol advancement.
</description>
*)
TYPE PULSE_TRAIN_INPUT_CHANNEL :
STRUCT
	Status AT %I* : WORD;
	//! <summary>ENC status from 0x1A05: counter-set acknowledgement bit 2, underflow 3 and overflow 4.</summary>
	CounterStatus AT %I* : WORD;
	//! <summary>32-bit feedback at 0x6020:11 from ENC Status PDO 0x1A05.</summary>
	CounterValue AT %I* : UDINT;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>
